1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,350
This is Spore, by SporeLabs.

2
00:00:02,650 --> 00:00:06,680
Video AI fails quietly on the conditions your cameras rarely see.

3
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:11,085
Spore finds where your video AI is weak, grows the data to cover it,

4
00:00:11,085 --> 00:00:13,440
and tests your models on it, in a loop.

5
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:17,270
First, it looks through everything you have.

6
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:22,217
Spore reads all six hundred twelve real clips indexed in VAST's video search,

7
00:00:22,217 --> 00:00:24,390
each with its Cosmos Reason caption.

8
00:00:25,990 --> 00:00:27,410
Then it finds the weak spots.

9
00:00:27,710 --> 00:00:31,090
These are live VSS searches against the highway cameras.

10
00:00:31,390 --> 00:00:33,050
Thirty clips in clear daylight.

11
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:34,300
Zero at night.

12
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:35,890
Zero in heavy rain.

13
00:00:36,190 --> 00:00:37,150
Zero in fog.

14
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:38,340
Zero in snow.

15
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:42,260
The detector on these cameras has never been tested in any of it.

16
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:47,284
An LLM on W&B Inference ranks which gaps matter,

17
00:00:47,284 --> 00:00:49,710
and every call is traced in Weave.

18
00:00:50,010 --> 00:00:51,390
Dense fog goes first.

19
00:00:51,690 --> 00:00:54,450
Glare, night, night rain and snow each get their own loop.

20
00:00:56,050 --> 00:00:59,020
Next, it grows the missing weather onto a real clip.

21
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:02,440
A physics weather layer adds fog, rain and snow,

22
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:05,560
and NVIDIA Cosmos Transfer turns day into night.

23
00:01:05,860 --> 00:01:08,980
The cars stay where they were, so we already know the right answer.

24
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:13,570
Then it tests the models inside the VSS pipeline.

25
00:01:13,870 --> 00:01:18,500
On this foggy clip, the Cosmos Reason caption model still counts twelve vehicles.

26
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:21,310
The YOLO detector misses six in ten cars.

27
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:24,830
Same clip, same pipeline, and the two models disagree.

28
00:01:26,430 --> 00:01:29,900
Across eleven clips and three severities, the pattern is clear.

29
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,586
In light fog, YOLO finds only four in

30
00:01:32,586 --> 00:01:34,650
ten cars a person can still see.

31
00:01:34,950 --> 00:01:37,540
In heavy fog or heavy rain, it finds one.

32
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:40,360
Every run is traced in W&B Weave.

33
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:44,730
And every frame Spore grows comes already labeled.

34
00:01:45,030 --> 00:01:49,776
The weather layer never moves a car, so the twenty-three boxes YOLO found on

35
00:01:49,776 --> 00:01:54,210
the clear-day frame line up exactly on the fog, rain and snow versions.

36
00:01:54,510 --> 00:01:59,499
That's nine hundred twenty-eight weather frames and nearly twelve thousand vehicle boxes

37
00:01:59,499 --> 00:02:02,220
for the Fix step, and not one was drawn by hand.

38
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:05,650
Then Spore picks the next weak spot.

39
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:09,190
Low sun glare held up: YOLO still finds eight in ten.

40
00:02:09,490 --> 00:02:11,130
Next up is the highway at night.

41
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:13,405
Find where your video AI is weak,

42
00:02:13,405 --> 00:02:15,680
grow the data to fix it, and go again.
